From c4b22549b82b9522d9c24c86af6ee533c81513bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chrg6 <chrg6@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:00:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Swing the shake key's stick by the game's updates instead of
 the clock, two updates a side at any frame rate.

shake_stick picked the side from the time since the press, 67 ms a side (two frames at the game's 30 fps), so above
30 fps each side lasted more of the game's updates: 8 at 120 fps and 16 at 240, slower swings than the game reads at
its own rate. The side now comes from the game's present count, which frame_rate.c already kept for the flight
recorder and now gives through frame_step_presents, two presents a side. The press still swings for 800 ms of the
clock and a hold keeps it going, as before; while no present comes (a load) the stick keeps its side.

Not reproduced before the change (read from the code). The new tests/shake_key_check.py builds shake_stick from
input.c and passes (it fails 118 times on the old code); the runtime compile check and the -Wall comparison of
input.c and frame_rate.c show no new warnings.

(cherry picked from upstream 5c9e480)
